WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Downloaded from RARBG

00:01:21.665 --> 00:01:26.670
I should've known that you would
be here, professor McGonagall.

00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:41.018
Good evening, professor Dumbledore.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.523
Are the rumors true, Albus?

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:52.029
I'm afraid so, professor.
The good and the bad.

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:55.490
- And the boy?
- Hagrid is bringing him.

00:01:55.741 --> 00:01:59.661
Is it wise to trust Hagrid
with something so important?

00:02:00.162 --> 00:02:04.666
Professor, I would trust Hagrid
with my life.

00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:28.065
Professor Dumbledore, sir.
Professor McGonagall.

00:02:28.273 --> 00:02:32.152
- No problems, I trust, Hagrid?
- No, sir.

00:02:32.361 --> 00:02:36.823
Little tyke fell asleep
as we were flying over Bristol.

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:40.077
Try not to wake him.

00:02:40.911 --> 00:02:42.996
There you go.

00:02:48.418 --> 00:02:52.923
Do you really think it's safe,
leaving him with these people?

00:02:53.298 --> 00:02:58.428
I've watched them all day.
They're the worst sort of Muggles.

00:02:58.679 --> 00:03:02.599
- They really are...
- The only family he has.

00:03:02.891 --> 00:03:07.813
He'll be famous. Every child
in our world will know his name.

00:03:08.063 --> 00:03:09.773
Exactly.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:14.277
He's far better off growing up
away from all of that.

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:19.449
Until he's ready.

00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:36.967
There, there, Hagrid.
It's not really goodbye, after all.

00:03:48.979 --> 00:03:50.480
Good luck...

00:03:51.523 --> 00:03:53.483
Harry Potter.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:14.129
Woman: Up. Get up!

00:04:31.897 --> 00:04:35.275
Dudley: Wake up, cousin!
We're going to the zoo!

00:04:46.453 --> 00:04:51.708
Petunia: Here comes the birthday boy.
Vernon: Happy birthday, son.

00:04:53.543 --> 00:04:56.713
Cook breakfast.
And try not to burn anything.

00:04:56.963 --> 00:05:01.927
- Yes, aunt Petunia.
- I want everything to be perfect...

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:05.055
For my Dudley's special day!

00:05:05.222 --> 00:05:10.227
- Hurry up! Bring my coffee, boy.
- Yes, uncle Vernon.

00:05:11.478 --> 00:05:14.564
Petunia:
Aren't they wonderful, darling?

00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:20.237
- How many are there?
- 36. Counted them myself.

00:05:20.487 --> 00:05:23.698
36?! But last year I had 37!

00:05:23.907 --> 00:05:27.744
- But some are bigger than last year's.
- I don't care!

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:30.497
This is what we're going to do.

00:05:30.705 --> 00:05:35.085
We're going to buy you two
new presents. How's that, pumpkin?

00:05:37.045 --> 00:05:42.384
Petunia: It should be a lovely day
at the 200. I'm looking forward to it.

00:05:45.971 --> 00:05:47.764
I'm warning you now, boy.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:51.518
Any funny business, any at all...

00:05:51.726 --> 00:05:54.771
And you won't have
any meals for a week.

00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:06.867
Dudley: Make it move.

00:06:09.536 --> 00:06:11.246
Move!

00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:13.957
- Move!
- He's asleep!

00:06:14.124 --> 00:06:16.710
He's boring.

00:06:19.129 --> 00:06:24.634
Sorry about him. He doesn't understand
what it's like, lying there...

00:06:25.093 --> 00:06:28.889
Watching people press
their ugly faces in on you.

00:06:31.641 --> 00:06:34.311
Can you hear me?

00:06:36.813 --> 00:06:40.817
It's just, I've never talked
to a snake before.

00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:42.736
Do you...?

00:06:42.944 --> 00:06:47.073
Do you talk to people often?

00:06:48.158 --> 00:06:51.494
You're from Burma, aren't you?
Was it nice there?

00:06:51.661 --> 00:06:53.997
Do you miss your family?

00:06:56.833 --> 00:07:01.588
I see. That's me as well.
I never knew my parents either.

00:07:01.796 --> 00:07:06.801
Mummy, dad, you won't believe
what this snake is doing!

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:33.536
Anytime.

00:07:36.873 --> 00:07:38.792
Man: Snake!

00:07:54.224 --> 00:07:57.602
Mum! Mummy! Help me!

00:07:57.852 --> 00:08:00.981
My darling boy!
How did you get in there?

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:06.569
Who did this? How did you get
in there? Is there a snake?

00:08:11.408 --> 00:08:16.746
It's all right, sweetheart.
We'll get you out of these cold clothes.

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:21.418
- What happened?
- I swear, I don't know!

00:08:21.626 --> 00:08:25.505
The glass was there
and then it was gone, like magic.

00:08:29.926 --> 00:08:32.721
There's no such thing as magic.

00:09:09.466 --> 00:09:12.177
Vernon:
Marge is ill. Ate a funny whelk.

00:09:12.385 --> 00:09:15.597
- Dad, look! Harry's got a letter!
- It's mine!

00:09:15.805 --> 00:09:18.558
Yours? Who'd be writing to you?

00:09:49.839 --> 00:09:54.344
Vernon:
No more mail through this letterbox.

00:10:06.523 --> 00:10:09.359
Petunia:
Have a lovely day at the office, dear.

00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:14.948
Shoo! Go on.

00:10:39.806 --> 00:10:42.684
Fine day, Sunday.

00:10:43.309 --> 00:10:47.981
In my opinion, best day of the week.
Why is that, Dudley?

00:10:48.189 --> 00:10:52.569
- Because there's no post on sundays?
- Right you are, Harry!

00:10:52.819 --> 00:10:55.572
No post on Sunday.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:00.910
Vernon:
No blasted letters today! No, sir.

00:11:01.494 --> 00:11:06.416
Not one single bloody letter. Not one!

00:11:14.883 --> 00:11:18.761
No, sir, not one blasted, miserable...

00:11:30.273 --> 00:11:32.442
Dudley: Make it stop, please!

00:11:34.277 --> 00:11:36.196
Vernon: Stop it!

00:11:40.325 --> 00:11:43.286
Mummy, what's happening?

00:11:46.706 --> 00:11:51.044
Give me that! Give me that letter!

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:55.423
Get off!

00:11:59.135 --> 00:12:03.348
They're my letters! Let go of me!

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.143
That's it! We're going away!

00:12:07.852 --> 00:12:11.481
Far away, where they can't find us!

00:12:11.731 --> 00:12:14.984
Daddy's gone mad, hasn't he?

00:12:49.894 --> 00:12:52.188
Make a wish, Harry.

00:13:08.288 --> 00:13:10.331
Who's there?

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:24.929
Sorry about that.

00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:36.399
I demand that you leave at once.
You are breaking and entering.

00:13:39.235 --> 00:13:42.071
Dry up, dursley, you great prune.

00:13:47.327 --> 00:13:50.830
I haven't seen you
since you was a baby, Harry.

00:13:51.039 --> 00:13:55.585
You're a bit more along than I expected.
Particularly in the middle.

00:13:55.752 --> 00:13:58.588
I'm not Harry.

00:14:00.465 --> 00:14:04.177
- I am.
- Well, of course you are.

00:14:04.969 --> 00:14:06.554
Got something for you.

00:14:06.763 --> 00:14:12.352
Afraid I sat on it, but I imagine
it'll taste fine just the same.

00:14:14.854 --> 00:14:18.274
Baked it myself, words and all.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:24.864
Thank you.

00:14:25.114 --> 00:14:29.243
It's not every day your young man
turns 11, is it?

00:14:44.425 --> 00:14:48.554
Excuse me, but who are you?

00:14:48.763 --> 00:14:53.643
Rubeus Hagrid, keeper of keys
and grounds at Hogwarts.

00:14:53.935 --> 00:14:57.647
- Of course, you know about Hogwarts.
- Sorry, no.

00:14:58.231 --> 00:15:03.152
Didn't you ever wonder where
your mum and dad learned it all?

00:15:03.403 --> 00:15:04.779
Learned what?

00:15:04.987 --> 00:15:07.532
You're a wizard, Harry.

00:15:08.741 --> 00:15:10.785
- I'm a what?
- A wizard.

00:15:10.993 --> 00:15:14.038
A good one, I'd wager,
once you're trained up.

00:15:14.288 --> 00:15:17.166
No, you've made a mistake.
I mean...

00:15:17.333 --> 00:15:20.336
I can't be a wizard.

00:15:21.045 --> 00:15:25.800
I mean, I'm just Harry. Just Harry.

00:15:26.843 --> 00:15:30.847
Well, just Harry, did you ever
make anything happen?

00:15:31.097 --> 00:15:35.768
Anything you couldn't explain,
when you were angry or scared?

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:55.288
Harry: "Dear Mr. Potter,
we are pleased to accept you...

00:15:55.496 --> 00:15:58.708
At Hogwarts school
of witchcraft and wizardry."

00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:03.880
He will not be going! We swore
we'd put a stop to all this rubbish.

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:08.342
You knew? You knew all along
and you never told me?

00:16:08.551 --> 00:16:11.637
Of course we knew.
How could you not be?

00:16:11.846 --> 00:16:15.558
My perfect sister being who she was.

00:16:15.725 --> 00:16:21.731
My mother and father were so proud
the day she got her letter.

00:16:21.898 --> 00:16:26.110
"We have a witch in the family.
Isn't it wonderful?"

00:16:26.319 --> 00:16:29.989
I was the only one to see her
for what she was.

00:16:30.198 --> 00:16:31.908
A freak!

00:16:32.158 --> 00:16:35.119
Then she met that Potter,
and then she had you...

00:16:35.328 --> 00:16:41.042
And I knew you would be the same.
Just as strange, just as abnormal.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:46.255
And then she got herself blown up,
and we got landed with you.

00:16:46.422 --> 00:16:50.426
Blown up? You told me
my parents died in a car crash.

00:16:50.718 --> 00:16:55.014
A car crash? A car crash killed
Lily and James Potter?

00:16:55.223 --> 00:16:59.143
- Petunia: We had to say something.
- It's an outrage! A scandal!

00:16:59.352 --> 00:17:01.771
He'll not be going.

00:17:02.021 --> 00:17:05.358
A great muggle like you
is going to stop him?

00:17:05.525 --> 00:17:06.567
Muggle?

00:17:06.901 --> 00:17:10.905
Non-magic folk. This boy's had
his name down since he were born.

00:17:11.113 --> 00:17:14.951
He's going to the finest school
of witchcraft and wizardry.

00:17:15.201 --> 00:17:21.123
He'll be under the finest headmaster
Hogwarts has seen, Albus Dumbledore.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:26.128
I will not pay to have a crackpot
old fool teach him magic tricks.

00:17:26.295 --> 00:17:30.883
Never insult Albus Dumbledore...

00:17:31.092 --> 00:17:33.135
In front of me.

00:17:50.987 --> 00:17:56.284
I'd appreciate it if you didn't tell
anyone at Hogwarts about that.

00:17:56.492 --> 00:18:00.621
- I'm not allowed to do magic.
- Okay.

00:18:01.914 --> 00:18:04.917
We're a bit behind schedule.
Best be off.

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:14.302
Unless you'd rather stay, of course.

00:18:29.358 --> 00:18:31.861
Harry:
"All students must be equipped with...

00:18:32.111 --> 00:18:35.031
One standard size 2
pewter cauldron...

00:18:35.239 --> 00:18:41.037
And may bring, if they desire,
either an owl, a cat or a toad."

00:18:41.287 --> 00:18:43.873
Can we find all this in London?

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:46.459
If you know where to go.

00:19:09.231 --> 00:19:12.193
Ah, Hagrid! The usual, I presume?

00:19:12.401 --> 00:19:16.280
No, thanks, Tom.
I'm on official Hogwarts business.

00:19:16.489 --> 00:19:19.575
Just helping Harry buy
his school supplies.

00:19:19.825 --> 00:19:23.371
Bless my soul. It's Harry Potter!

00:19:27.667 --> 00:19:31.087
Welcome back, Mr. Potter.
Welcome back.

00:19:31.337 --> 00:19:35.675
Doris crockford. I can't believe
I'm meeting you at last.

00:19:36.092 --> 00:19:41.389
Harry Potter. Can't tell you
how pleased I am to meet you.

00:19:41.597 --> 00:19:44.100
Hello, professor. I didn't see you.

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:49.355
Professor quirrell will be your
defense against the dark arts teacher.

00:19:49.563 --> 00:19:51.941
Oh, nice to meet you.

00:19:52.233 --> 00:19:55.319
Fearfully fascinating subject.

00:19:55.528 --> 00:20:00.116
Not that you need it, eh, Potter?

00:20:01.075 --> 00:20:05.246
Yes, well, must be going now.
Lots to buy.

00:20:05.454 --> 00:20:07.206
Harry: Goodbye.

00:20:09.917 --> 00:20:13.462
- See, Harry? You're famous.
- But why am I famous?

00:20:13.713 --> 00:20:17.133
All those people,
how is it they know who I am?

00:20:17.383 --> 00:20:21.137
I'm not sure I'm the right person
to tell you that.

00:20:38.154 --> 00:20:41.949
Welcome, Harry, to diagon alley.

00:20:58.299 --> 00:21:00.801
Here, you get your quills and ink.

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:04.972
Over there, all your bits and Bobs
for doing wizardry.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:32.041
Boy 1:
It's a world-class racing broom.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:39.715
Boy 2:
It's the fastest model yet.

00:21:43.427 --> 00:21:48.015
But how am I to pay for all this?
I haven't any money.

00:21:48.224 --> 00:21:51.560
There's your money.
Gringotts, the wizard bank.

00:21:51.811 --> 00:21:57.316
Ain't no safer place, not one.
Except perhaps Hogwarts.

00:22:09.954 --> 00:22:13.958
Hagrid, what exactly are these things?

00:22:14.166 --> 00:22:19.421
They're goblins. Clever as they come,
but not the most friendly of beasts.

00:22:19.588 --> 00:22:21.590
Best stay close.

00:22:25.594 --> 00:22:29.265
Mr. Harry Potter wishes
to make a withdrawal.

00:22:33.519 --> 00:22:36.689
And does Mr. Harry Potter
have his key?

00:22:37.606 --> 00:22:40.860
Wait a minute.
Got it here somewhere.

00:22:46.740 --> 00:22:49.618
And there's something else as well.

00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:54.206
Professor Dumbledore gave me this.

00:22:58.252 --> 00:23:03.299
It's about you-know-what
in vault you-know-which.

00:23:04.633 --> 00:23:06.594
Very well.

00:23:16.562 --> 00:23:18.814
Lamp, please.

00:23:27.323 --> 00:23:28.657
Key, please.

00:23:52.139 --> 00:23:55.851
Did you think your parents
would leave you with nothing?

00:23:57.186 --> 00:24:00.856
Goblin: Vault 713.
Harry: What's in there, Hagrid?

00:24:01.106 --> 00:24:05.277
Hagrid: Can't tell you.
Hogwarts business. Very secret.

00:24:05.527 --> 00:24:07.071
Goblin: Stand back.

00:24:35.349 --> 00:24:38.143
Best not to mention this to anyone.

00:24:46.568 --> 00:24:50.489
I still need a wand.

00:24:50.698 --> 00:24:54.118
You want ollivanders.
There ain't no place better.

00:24:54.827 --> 00:24:59.915
Run along there and wait.
I got one more thing to do.

00:25:17.933 --> 00:25:19.768
Hello?

00:25:22.730 --> 00:25:24.565
Hello?

00:25:28.068 --> 00:25:32.364
I wondered when
I'd be seeing you, Mr. Potter.

00:25:40.164 --> 00:25:42.374
It seems only yesterday...

00:25:42.624 --> 00:25:48.464
That your mother and father were
in here buying their first wands.

00:25:55.137 --> 00:25:57.431
Here we are.

00:26:05.981 --> 00:26:08.567
Give it a wave.

00:26:14.990 --> 00:26:17.576
Apparently not.

00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:27.211
Perhaps...

00:26:28.837 --> 00:26:31.006
This.

00:26:38.097 --> 00:26:42.726
No, no, definitely not. No matter.

00:26:49.942 --> 00:26:51.527
I wonder...

00:27:20.764 --> 00:27:23.058
Curious.

00:27:23.267 --> 00:27:26.186
Very curious.

00:27:26.395 --> 00:27:29.523
Sorry, but what's curious?

00:27:31.233 --> 00:27:34.528
I remember every wand
I've ever sold, Mr. Potter.

00:27:34.736 --> 00:27:37.489
It so happens that the Phoenix...

00:27:37.698 --> 00:27:42.411
Whose tail feather resides
in your wand, gave another feather.

00:27:42.828 --> 00:27:45.914
Just one other.

00:27:46.081 --> 00:27:50.419
It is curious that you should
be destined for this wand...

00:27:50.711 --> 00:27:56.383
When its brother gave you that scar.

00:27:58.218 --> 00:28:01.430
And who owned that wand?

00:28:02.264 --> 00:28:04.683
We do not speak his name.

00:28:05.100 --> 00:28:08.604
The wand chooses
the wizard, Mr. Potter.

00:28:08.854 --> 00:28:11.857
It's not always clear why.

00:28:12.232 --> 00:28:15.736
But I think it is clear...

00:28:15.944 --> 00:28:19.865
That we can expect
great things from you.

00:28:20.073 --> 00:28:24.328
After all, he-who-must-not-be-named...

00:28:24.578 --> 00:28:27.247
Did great things.

00:28:27.456 --> 00:28:29.458
Terrible...

00:28:29.917 --> 00:28:33.128
Yes, but great.

00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:40.844
Hagrid: Harry! Harry!

00:28:41.220 --> 00:28:43.597
Happy birthday.

00:28:45.098 --> 00:28:46.141
Harry:

00:28:50.729 --> 00:28:54.233
You all right, Harry?
You seem very quiet.

00:28:54.608 --> 00:29:00.155
He killed my parents, didn't he?
The one who gave me this.

00:29:00.405 --> 00:29:03.992
You know, Hagrid. I know you do.

00:29:07.913 --> 00:29:12.459
First, and understand this
because it's very important:

00:29:12.668 --> 00:29:15.170
Not all wizards are good.

00:29:15.420 --> 00:29:17.923
Some of them go bad.
A few years ago...

00:29:18.131 --> 00:29:23.136
There was a wizard who went as bad
as you can go. His name was v...

00:29:23.345 --> 00:29:26.974
- His name was v...
- Maybe if you wrote it down?

00:29:27.182 --> 00:29:29.017
No, I can't spell it.

00:29:29.268 --> 00:29:33.522
- All right, Voldemort.
- Voldemort?

00:29:33.689 --> 00:29:36.149
Shh.

00:29:37.484 --> 00:29:39.695
It was dark times, Harry.

00:29:42.030 --> 00:29:45.158
Voldemort started
to gather some followers.

00:29:45.409 --> 00:29:48.704
Brought them over to the dark side.

00:29:50.122 --> 00:29:53.208
Anyone that stood up to him
ended up dead.

00:29:54.376 --> 00:29:57.421
Your parents fought against him.

00:29:57.629 --> 00:30:01.425
But nobody lived once
he decided to kill them.

00:30:05.804 --> 00:30:08.390
Nobody, not one.

00:30:08.557 --> 00:30:10.976
Except you.

00:30:12.978 --> 00:30:17.065
Me? Voldemort tried to kill me?

00:30:17.566 --> 00:30:21.737
Yes. That ain't no ordinary cut
on your forehead, Harry.

00:30:22.029 --> 00:30:27.743
A Mark like that only comes from being
touched by a curse, an evil curse.

00:30:27.993 --> 00:30:31.580
What happened to v...?
To you-know-who?

00:30:32.748 --> 00:30:36.084
Well, some say he died.

00:30:36.335 --> 00:30:38.754
Codswallop, in my opinion.

00:30:38.962 --> 00:30:42.215
Nope, I reckon he's out there still...

00:30:42.424 --> 00:30:45.385
Too tired to carry on.

00:30:45.594 --> 00:30:51.016
But one thing's certain. Something
about you stumped him that night.

00:30:51.266 --> 00:30:55.520
That's why you're famous.
That's why everybody knows your name.

00:30:55.979 --> 00:30:59.608
You're the boy who lived.

00:31:08.992 --> 00:31:11.703
What are you looking at?
00:31:13.455 --> 00:31:15.457
Blimey, is that the time?

00:31:15.624 --> 00:31:19.628
I'm gonna have to leave you.
Dumbledore will be wanting his...

00:31:19.878 --> 00:31:24.758
Well, he'll be wanting to see me.
Your train leaves in 10 minutes.

00:31:24.966 --> 00:31:30.305
Here's your ticket. Stick to your ticket,
that's very important.

00:31:33.141 --> 00:31:35.435
"Platform 9 3/4"?

00:31:35.644 --> 00:31:40.440
But, Hagrid, there must be a mistake.
This says platform 9 3/4.

00:31:40.649 --> 00:31:43.985
There's no such thing, is there?

00:32:02.504 --> 00:32:04.089
Man: Sorry.

00:32:05.590 --> 00:32:08.343
Excuse me. Excuse me.

00:32:08.552 --> 00:32:10.095
On your left.

00:32:10.345 --> 00:32:14.141
Can you tell me where
I might find platform 9 3/4?

00:32:14.349 --> 00:32:16.852
Think you're being funny, do you?

00:32:17.102 --> 00:32:20.439
Mrs. Weasley: It's the same
every year, packed with Muggles.

00:32:20.856 --> 00:32:24.276
- Muggles?
- Mrs. Weasley: Platform 9 3/4, this way.

00:32:29.948 --> 00:32:33.118
All right, Percy, you first.

00:32:43.086 --> 00:32:44.296
Fred, you next.

00:32:44.504 --> 00:32:48.216
- He's not Fred, I am.
- You call yourself our mother?

00:32:48.383 --> 00:32:50.385
I'm sorry, George.

00:32:54.514 --> 00:32:56.892
I'm onlyjoking. I am Fred.

00:33:02.731 --> 00:33:05.317
Excuse me.

00:33:06.401 --> 00:33:09.196
Could you tell me how to...?

00:33:09.404 --> 00:33:12.908
How to get onto the platform?
Not to worry, dear.

00:33:13.158 --> 00:33:15.619
It's Ron's first time
to Hogwarts as well.

00:33:15.827 --> 00:33:21.750
All you do is walk straight at the wall
between platforms 9 and 10.

00:33:21.917 --> 00:33:25.420
- Best to run if you're nervous.
- Good luck.

00:34:22.978 --> 00:34:27.274
Excuse me. Do you mind?
Everywhere else is full.

00:34:32.779 --> 00:34:35.198
I'm Ron, by the way. Ron Weasley.

00:34:35.448 --> 00:34:38.076
I'm Harry. Harry Potter.

00:34:39.452 --> 00:34:41.496
So it's true!

00:34:41.705 --> 00:34:44.499
I mean, do you really have the...?

00:34:45.083 --> 00:34:47.961
- The what?
- The scar?

00:34:48.461 --> 00:34:50.505
Oh, yeah.

00:34:55.802 --> 00:35:00.974
- Anything off the trolley, dears?
- No, thanks. I'm all set.

00:35:05.020 --> 00:35:07.314
We'll take the lot.

00:35:18.033 --> 00:35:22.829
- Bertie bott's every flavor beans?
- They mean every flavor.

00:35:23.246 --> 00:35:26.625
There's chocolate
and peppermint and also...

00:35:26.833 --> 00:35:30.670
Spinach, liver and tripe.

00:35:30.879 --> 00:35:35.050
George sweared he got
a booger-flavored one once.

00:35:39.721 --> 00:35:45.060
- Are they real frogs?
- It's a spell. You want the cards.

00:35:45.268 --> 00:35:50.732
Each pack's got a famous witch
or wizard. I've got about 500 meself.

00:35:56.529 --> 00:36:00.325
That's rotten luck. They've only
got one good jump in them.

00:36:03.203 --> 00:36:07.082
- I've got Dumbledore!
- I got about six of him.

00:36:08.875 --> 00:36:10.418
Hey, he's gone!

00:36:10.585 --> 00:36:14.089
You can't expect him to
hang around all day, can you?

00:36:14.714 --> 00:36:17.842
This is scabbers. Pathetic, isn't he?

00:36:18.051 --> 00:36:19.219
A little.

00:36:19.427 --> 00:36:22.764
Fred gave me a spell
to turn him yellow. Want to see?

00:36:31.773 --> 00:36:33.400
Has anyone seen a toad?

00:36:33.775 --> 00:36:36.444
- A boy named Neville's lost one.
- No.

00:36:37.028 --> 00:36:41.366
Oh, are you doing magic?
Let's see, then.

00:36:42.409 --> 00:36:46.746
Sunshine, daisies, butter mellow

00:36:46.955 --> 00:36:50.083
turn this stupid, fat rat yellow

00:36:52.836 --> 00:36:58.466
are you sure that's a real spell?
Well, it's not very good, is it?

00:36:58.633 --> 00:37:01.928
I've only tried
a few simple ones myself...

00:37:02.137 --> 00:37:04.764
But they've all worked for me.

00:37:08.393 --> 00:37:10.437
For example:

00:37:10.812 --> 00:37:13.606
Oculus reparo.

00:37:15.650 --> 00:37:18.319
That's better, isn't it?

00:37:19.487 --> 00:37:23.408
Holy cricket, you're Harry Potter!

00:37:23.616 --> 00:37:27.162
I'm Hermione Granger.
And you are...?

00:37:27.912 --> 00:37:31.124
- I'm Ron Weasley.
- Pleasure.

00:37:31.332 --> 00:37:36.421
You two better change into robes.
I expect we'll be arriving soon.

00:37:40.508 --> 00:37:44.012
You've got dirt on your nose.
Did you know?

00:37:44.179 --> 00:37:46.181
Just there.

00:37:58.526 --> 00:38:02.322
Right, then.
First years, this way, please!

00:38:02.530 --> 00:38:07.702
Come on, first years, don't be shy.
Come on now, hurry up.

00:38:14.709 --> 00:38:17.712
- Hello, Harry.
- Hi, Hagrid.

00:38:19.130 --> 00:38:23.134
Right, then. This way to the boats.
Come on now, follow me.

00:39:38.793 --> 00:39:41.045
Welcome to Hogwarts.

00:39:41.254 --> 00:39:45.258
Shortly, you'll pass through
these doors and join your classmates.

00:39:45.466 --> 00:39:50.513
But before you take your seats,
you must be sorted into your houses.

00:39:50.722 --> 00:39:53.808
They are Gryffindor, hufflepuff...

00:39:54.058 --> 00:39:58.521
Ravenclaw and Slytherin.

00:39:58.938 --> 00:40:03.985
While you're here, your house
will be like your family.

00:40:04.611 --> 00:40:08.114
Your triumphs will earn you points.

00:40:08.323 --> 00:40:12.452
Any rule-breaking
and you will lose points.

00:40:12.660 --> 00:40:17.957
At the end of the year, the house with
the most points wins the house cup.

00:40:18.166 --> 00:40:19.500
Trevor!

00:40:28.426 --> 00:40:30.053
Sorry.

00:40:30.261 --> 00:40:34.182
The sorting ceremony
will begin momentarily.

00:40:35.558 --> 00:40:38.853
It's true then,
what they're saying on the train.

00:40:39.312 --> 00:40:41.940
Harry Potter has come to Hogwarts.

00:40:42.148 --> 00:40:43.566
Harry Potter?

00:40:44.192 --> 00:40:46.861
This is crabbe and goyle.

00:40:47.070 --> 00:40:49.364
And I'm Malfoy.

00:40:49.697 --> 00:40:52.033
Draco Malfoy.

00:40:53.993 --> 00:40:57.580
Think my name's funny, do you?
I've no need to ask yours.

00:40:57.789 --> 00:41:03.586
Red hair and a hand-me-down robe?
You must be a Weasley.

00:41:04.504 --> 00:41:08.549
You'll find out some wizarding families
are better than others.

00:41:08.716 --> 00:41:12.553
You don't want to go making friends
with the wrong sort.

00:41:12.720 --> 00:41:14.889
I can help you there.

00:41:17.141 --> 00:41:20.979
I think I can tell the wrong sort
for myself, thanks.

00:41:26.609 --> 00:41:28.820
We're ready for you now.
Follow me.

00:41:47.422 --> 00:41:51.926
The ceiling isn't real. It's bewitched
to look like the night sky.

00:41:52.260 --> 00:41:55.138
I read about it
in Hogwarts, a history.

00:42:08.401 --> 00:42:11.237
Will you wait along here, please?

00:42:12.655 --> 00:42:15.450
Now, before we begin...

00:42:15.658 --> 00:42:18.911
Professor Dumbledore would like
to say a few words.

00:42:19.120 --> 00:42:23.916
I have a few start-of-term notices
I wish to announce.

00:42:24.292 --> 00:42:26.419
The first years, please note...

00:42:26.711 --> 00:42:32.717
That the dark forest is
strictly forbidden to all students.

00:42:32.967 --> 00:42:38.473
Also, our caretaker, Mr. Filch,
has asked me to remind you...

00:42:38.681 --> 00:42:43.311
That the third-floor corridor
is out of bounds...

00:42:43.603 --> 00:42:47.815
To everyone who does not wish
to die a most painful death.

00:42:49.192 --> 00:42:51.152
Thank you.

00:42:52.904 --> 00:42:56.991
When I call your name,
you will come forth.

00:42:57.200 --> 00:43:00.828
I shall place the sorting hat
on your head...

00:43:00.995 --> 00:43:04.248
And you will be sorted
into your houses.

00:43:04.457 --> 00:43:07.085
Hermione Granger.

00:43:09.337 --> 00:43:11.964
Oh, no. Okay, relax.

00:43:12.340 --> 00:43:15.718
Mental, that one, I'm telling you.

00:43:20.223 --> 00:43:25.019
Ah, right, then. Mm, right.

00:43:25.269 --> 00:43:28.856
Okay. Gryffindor!

00:43:37.657 --> 00:43:40.451
Draco Malfoy.

00:43:44.997 --> 00:43:47.208
Slytherin!

00:43:48.167 --> 00:43:51.045
Every wizard who went bad
was in Slytherin.

00:43:51.295 --> 00:43:53.840
Susan bones.

00:44:00.805 --> 00:44:02.223
Ah!

00:44:02.390 --> 00:44:04.517
Harry, what is it?

00:44:04.767 --> 00:44:07.478
Nothing. Nothing, I'm fine.

00:44:07.728 --> 00:44:09.147
Sorting hat: Let's see...

00:44:09.397 --> 00:44:13.734
I know! Hufflepuff!

00:44:15.486 --> 00:44:17.905
Ronald Weasley.

00:44:30.751 --> 00:44:36.757
Ha, another Weasley!
I know just what to do with you.

00:44:37.425 --> 00:44:39.760
Gryffindor!

00:44:45.933 --> 00:44:48.436
Harry Potter.

00:45:05.578 --> 00:45:09.540
Hm, difficult, very difficult.

00:45:09.749 --> 00:45:13.711
Plenty of courage, I see.
Not a bad mind, either.

00:45:13.920 --> 00:45:16.214
There's talent, oh, yes.

00:45:16.422 --> 00:45:20.259
And a thirst to prove yourself.

00:45:20.468 --> 00:45:22.637
But where to put you?

00:45:23.221 --> 00:45:25.723
Not Slytherin, not Slytherin!

00:45:25.973 --> 00:45:29.602
Not Slytherin, eh? Are you sure?

00:45:29.810 --> 00:45:34.649
You could be great, you know.
It's all here, in your head.

00:45:34.899 --> 00:45:40.238
And Slytherin will help you on the way
to greatness, no doubt about that.

00:45:40.571 --> 00:45:45.159
- No? Well, if you're sure.
- Please, no.

00:45:47.370 --> 00:45:49.330
Gryffindor!

00:46:14.855 --> 00:46:17.650
Your attention, please.

00:46:19.694 --> 00:46:22.405
Let the feast begin.

00:46:39.338 --> 00:46:40.881
I'm half and half.

00:46:41.048 --> 00:46:44.343
Me dad's a muggle. Mum's a witch.

00:46:44.552 --> 00:46:48.055
Bit of a nasty shock for him
when he found out.

00:46:49.056 --> 00:46:52.852
Percy, who's that teacher
talking to professor ouirrell?

00:46:53.185 --> 00:46:56.314
Percy: Professor Snape,
head of Slytherin house.

00:46:56.522 --> 00:46:58.441
- What's he teach?
- Pofions.

00:46:58.649 --> 00:47:04.238
But he fancies the dark arts.
He's been after ouirrell's job for years.

00:47:08.743 --> 00:47:11.078
Hello! How are you?

00:47:11.329 --> 00:47:14.707
Welcome to Gryffindor.

00:47:24.759 --> 00:47:27.261
Girl: It's the bloody baron!

00:47:31.932 --> 00:47:34.727
Hello, sir Nicholas.
Have a nice summer?

00:47:34.935 --> 00:47:40.358
Dismal. Once again, my request to join
the headless hunt has been denied.

00:47:43.402 --> 00:47:46.280
I know you.
You're nearly headless Nick.

00:47:46.530 --> 00:47:49.283
I prefer sir Nicholas,
if you don't mind.

00:47:49.492 --> 00:47:52.995
"Nearly" headless?
How can you be nearly headless?

00:48:05.299 --> 00:48:09.136
Percy: Gryffindors, follow me, please.
Keep up. Thank you.

00:48:09.303 --> 00:48:13.641
Ravenclaw, follow me. This way.

00:48:13.933 --> 00:48:17.269
Percy: This is the most direct path
to the dormitories.

00:48:17.478 --> 00:48:21.649
Keep an eye on the staircases.
They like to change.

00:48:30.783 --> 00:48:36.580
Keep up, please, and follow me.
Quickly now, come on. Come on.

00:48:36.789 --> 00:48:39.458
Ron: That picture's moving.

00:48:39.667 --> 00:48:43.170
Ron: Look at that one.
Harry: I think she fancies you.

00:48:44.922 --> 00:48:47.258
Girl 1: Look!
Girl 2: Who's that girl?

00:48:47.466 --> 00:48:50.010
Man in picture:
Welcome to Hogwarts.

00:48:51.679 --> 00:48:52.763
Girl 3: Who's that?

00:49:06.026 --> 00:49:07.611
Password?

00:49:08.070 --> 00:49:10.865
Caput draconis.

00:49:17.621 --> 00:49:22.501
Percy: Follow me, everyone.
Keep up. Quickly, come on.

00:49:25.212 --> 00:49:27.631
Gather around here.

00:49:29.341 --> 00:49:32.636
Welcome to the Gryffindor
common room.

00:49:32.845 --> 00:49:37.224
Boys' dormitory is upstairs to the left.
Girls, the same on your right.

00:49:37.475 --> 00:49:40.603
Your belongings have
already been brought up.

00:50:50.631 --> 00:50:55.052
Can you imagine the look on old
McGonagall's face if we were late?

00:50:58.305 --> 00:51:03.269
- That was bloody brilliant!
- Thank you for that assessment.

00:51:03.477 --> 00:51:07.773
It'd be better if I transfigured
Mr. Potter and you into a watch.

00:51:07.982 --> 00:51:11.193
- Then one of you might be on time.
- We got lost.

00:51:11.402 --> 00:51:17.157
Then perhaps a map? I trust you
don't need one to find your seats.

00:51:25.332 --> 00:51:31.005
There will be no foolish wand-waving
or silly incantations in this class.

00:51:31.213 --> 00:51:34.842
As such, I don't expect
many of you to appreciate...

00:51:35.092 --> 00:51:38.804
The subtle science and exact art
that is potion-making.

00:51:39.013 --> 00:51:42.099
However, for those select few...

00:51:43.017 --> 00:51:46.353
Who possess the predisposition...

00:51:50.024 --> 00:51:53.319
I can teach you
how to bewitch the mind...

00:51:53.527 --> 00:51:56.447
And ensnare the senses.

00:51:56.655 --> 00:51:59.199
I can tell you how to bottle fame...

00:51:59.366 --> 00:52:05.331
Brew glory and even
put a stopper in death.

00:52:09.376 --> 00:52:14.256
Then again, maybe some of you have
come to Hogwarts with abilities...

00:52:14.465 --> 00:52:20.387
So formidable that
you feel confident enough...

00:52:20.638 --> 00:52:23.557
To not pay attention.

00:52:33.359 --> 00:52:37.196
Our new celebrity.

00:52:39.365 --> 00:52:45.162
What would I get if I added root of
asphodel to an infusion of wormwood?

00:52:48.415 --> 00:52:50.834
You don't know? Let's try again.

00:52:51.043 --> 00:52:55.673
Where would you look
if I asked you to find a bezoar?

00:52:56.924 --> 00:52:58.342
I don't know, sir.

00:52:58.592 --> 00:53:02.429
Snape: What is the difference
between monkshood and wolfsbane?

00:53:05.015 --> 00:53:07.267
I don't know, sir.

00:53:08.352 --> 00:53:09.603
Pity.

00:53:11.355 --> 00:53:15.567
Clearly, fame isn't everything...

00:53:16.276 --> 00:53:17.277
Is it, Mr. Potter?

00:53:21.281 --> 00:53:26.912
Eye of rabbit, harp string hum
turn this water into rum

00:53:28.122 --> 00:53:29.623
eye of rabbit...

00:53:29.957 --> 00:53:32.626
What's Seamus trying to do
to the water?

00:53:32.918 --> 00:53:37.631
Turn it to rum. Actually managed
a weak tea yesterday, before...

00:53:44.138 --> 00:53:46.265
Mail's here.

00:54:18.505 --> 00:54:21.508
Can I borrow this? Thanks.

00:54:25.429 --> 00:54:27.639
Look, Neville's got a remembrall.

00:54:27.848 --> 00:54:33.353
I've read about those. The smoke turns
red when you've forgotten something.

00:54:33.687 --> 00:54:37.024
The problem is, I can't remember
what I've forgotten.

00:54:37.357 --> 00:54:40.778
Somebody broke into gringotts. Listen.

00:54:40.986 --> 00:54:44.656
"Believed to be the work
of dark wizards or witches...

00:54:44.907 --> 00:54:50.621
Gringotts goblins acknowledge
the breach but insist nothing was taken.

00:54:50.829 --> 00:54:56.543
The vault in question, number 713,
had been emptied earlier that same day."

00:54:56.710 --> 00:55:01.006
That's odd. That's the vault
Hagrid and I went to.

00:55:09.932 --> 00:55:13.685
- Good afternoon, class.
- Good afternoon, madam hooch.

00:55:13.894 --> 00:55:16.688
Good afternoon, Amanda.
Good afternoon.

00:55:17.981 --> 00:55:20.442
Welcome to your first flying lesson.

00:55:20.651 --> 00:55:24.571
What are you waiting for?
Step up to your broomstick.

00:55:24.738 --> 00:55:30.369
Come on now, hurry up. Stick your hand
over the broom and say, "up."

00:55:38.752 --> 00:55:40.379
Up. Up!

00:55:40.587 --> 00:55:42.589
With feeling.

00:55:42.756 --> 00:55:43.841
All: Up!

00:55:48.387 --> 00:55:50.347
Up! Om

00:55:51.265 --> 00:55:53.392
shut up, Harry.

00:55:53.600 --> 00:55:58.272
Now, once you've got hold of
your broom, I want you to mount it.

00:55:58.480 --> 00:56:02.484
Grip it tight. You don't wanna be
sliding off the end.

00:56:02.860 --> 00:56:07.781
When I blow my whistle, I want you
to kick off from the ground, hard.

00:56:08.031 --> 00:56:11.869
Keep your broom steady,
hover for a moment...

00:56:12.077 --> 00:56:16.373
Then lean fonnard slightly
and touch back down.

00:56:16.623 --> 00:56:19.751
On my whistle. Three, two...

00:56:22.129 --> 00:56:23.547
Mr. Longbottom.

00:56:28.135 --> 00:56:31.054
- Mr. Longbottom!
- Down, down!

00:56:31.263 --> 00:56:32.514
Neville!

00:56:36.226 --> 00:56:38.896
Come back down this instant!

00:56:48.822 --> 00:56:51.325
Mr. Longbo...

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:02.753
Neville: Whoa!

00:57:07.841 --> 00:57:10.260
Madam hooch:
Everyone out of the way!

00:57:15.807 --> 00:57:17.976
Is he all right?

00:57:18.352 --> 00:57:24.024
Oh, dear, it's a broken wrist.
Poor boy. Come on now, up you get.

00:57:25.317 --> 00:57:29.988
Keep your feet on the ground
while I take him to the hospital wing.

00:57:30.197 --> 00:57:33.867
Understand? If I see
a single broom in the air...

00:57:34.076 --> 00:57:39.331
The one riding it will be expelled
before they can say ouidditch.

00:57:39.539 --> 00:57:41.458
Did you see his face?

00:57:41.667 --> 00:57:45.504
If he had squeezed this, he'd have
remembered to fall on his arse.

00:57:45.712 --> 00:57:48.215
Give it here, Malfoy.

00:57:49.049 --> 00:57:52.719
No. I'll leave it somewhere
for Longbottom to find.

00:57:56.890 --> 00:57:59.393
How about on the roof?

00:58:00.560 --> 00:58:04.398
What's the matter, Potter?
Bit beyond your reach?

00:58:06.900 --> 00:58:10.737
Harry, no way!
You heard what madam hooch said.

00:58:10.904 --> 00:58:13.865
Besides, you don't know how to fly.

00:58:19.413 --> 00:58:22.916
Give it here or I'll
knock you off your broom!

00:58:23.166 --> 00:58:25.252
Is that so?

00:58:28.422 --> 00:58:30.716
Have it your way, then.

00:59:03.457 --> 00:59:07.085
Boy 1: Nice going, Harry.
Boy 2: That was wicked, Harry!

00:59:07.294 --> 00:59:09.296
Harry Potter!

00:59:10.297 --> 00:59:12.299
Follow me.

00:59:23.977 --> 00:59:26.229
You wait here.

00:59:27.981 --> 00:59:33.278
Professor quirrell, excuse me.Could I borrow wood for a moment?

00:59:33.487 --> 00:59:35.322
Yes, of course.

00:59:40.994 --> 00:59:46.750
Potter, this is Oliver wood.
Wood, I have found you a seeker.

00:59:48.835 --> 00:59:52.339
Have you heard? Harry Potter's
the new Gryffindor seeker.

00:59:52.589 --> 00:59:54.800
I always knew he'd do well.

00:59:55.258 --> 00:59:59.304
Seeker? But first years
never make the house teams.

00:59:59.513 --> 01:00:04.351
- You must be the youngest player in...
- A century, McGonagall says.

01:00:04.518 --> 01:00:06.853
Well done, Harry.
Wood's just told us.

01:00:07.020 --> 01:00:09.523
Fred and George are on the team.
Beaters.

01:00:09.773 --> 01:00:13.485
Our job is to make sure you
don't get bloodied up too bad.

01:00:13.693 --> 01:00:16.363
Can't make any promises.
Rough game, Quidditch.

01:00:16.530 --> 01:00:20.534
But no one's died in years.
Someone vanishes occasionally.

01:00:20.742 --> 01:00:23.495
But they'll turn up in a month or two.

01:00:23.745 --> 01:00:29.376
Go on. Quidditch is great. Best game
there is, and you'll be great too.

01:00:29.543 --> 01:00:32.796
I've never played.
What if I make a fool of myself?

01:00:33.213 --> 01:00:38.009
You won't make a fool of yourself.
It's in your blood.

01:00:46.560 --> 01:00:50.397
You never told me your father
was a seeker too.

01:00:57.904 --> 01:01:02.534
I'm telling you, it's spooky.
She knows more about you than you do.

01:01:02.742 --> 01:01:05.036
Harry: Who doesn't?

01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:08.081
What's happening?

01:01:08.290 --> 01:01:12.502
The staircases change, remember?

01:01:17.924 --> 01:01:22.429
- Let's go this way.
- Ron: Before the staircase moves again.

01:01:30.061 --> 01:01:33.440
Does anybody feel like
we shouldn't be here?

01:01:33.732 --> 01:01:35.859
Hermione:
We're not supposed to be here.

01:01:36.067 --> 01:01:39.946
This is the third floor.
It's forbidden.

01:01:41.114 --> 01:01:42.741
Let's go.

01:01:44.951 --> 01:01:47.829
Hermione: It's Filch's cat!
Harry: Run!

01:01:51.625 --> 01:01:54.961
Quick, let's hide through that door!

01:02:00.091 --> 01:02:02.135
- It's locked!
- We're done for!

01:02:02.344 --> 01:02:04.471
Move over!

01:02:05.472 --> 01:02:07.599
Alohomora.

01:02:11.645 --> 01:02:12.729
Alohomora?

01:02:12.938 --> 01:02:15.482
Standard book of spells,
chapter seven.

01:02:15.649 --> 01:02:19.069
Filch: Anyone here, my sweet?

01:02:25.283 --> 01:02:26.326
Come on.

01:02:27.118 --> 01:02:29.746
- Hermione: Filch is gone.
- He thinks this door's locked.

01:02:29.913 --> 01:02:33.500
- It was locked.
- And for good reason.

01:02:59.192 --> 01:03:04.698
What are they doing, keeping a thing
like that locked up in a school?

01:03:04.906 --> 01:03:08.535
Didn't you see what
it was standing on?

01:03:08.785 --> 01:03:12.956
I wasn't looking at its feet!
I was preoccupied with its heads.

01:03:13.164 --> 01:03:16.042
Or maybe you didn't notice.
There were three!

01:03:16.209 --> 01:03:19.921
Hermione: It was standing on
a trap door. It wasn't there by accident.

01:03:20.130 --> 01:03:23.675
- It's guarding something.
- Guarding something?

01:03:24.050 --> 01:03:27.846
That's right. Now, if you two
don't mind, I'm going to bed...

01:03:28.054 --> 01:03:31.683
Before you come up with another idea
to get us killed.

01:03:31.891 --> 01:03:35.020
Or worse, expelled.

01:03:38.231 --> 01:03:42.527
She needs to sort out her priorities.

01:03:47.157 --> 01:03:51.369
Quidditch is easy to understand.
Each team has seven players.

01:03:51.578 --> 01:03:57.250
Three chasers, two beaters,
one keeper and a seeker. That's you.

01:04:02.380 --> 01:04:06.509
There are three kinds of balls.
This one's called the quaffle.

01:04:06.718 --> 01:04:12.682
The chasers handle the quaffle and try
to put it through one of those hoops.

01:04:12.891 --> 01:04:17.270
The keeper, that's me,
defends the hoops. With me so far?

01:04:17.479 --> 01:04:21.941
I think so. What are those?

01:04:24.235 --> 01:04:26.404
You better take this.

01:04:36.456 --> 01:04:39.250
Careful now, it's coming back.

01:04:45.799 --> 01:04:49.469
Not bad, Potter.
You'd make a fair beater.

01:05:06.111 --> 01:05:08.405
What was that?

01:05:09.155 --> 01:05:12.909
Bludger. Nasty little buggers.

01:05:13.118 --> 01:05:16.621
But you are a seeker.

01:05:20.166 --> 01:05:24.796
The only thing I want you
to worry about is this.

01:05:25.046 --> 01:05:27.549
The golden snitch.

01:05:27.757 --> 01:05:30.760
- I like this ball.
- You like it now.

01:05:30.969 --> 01:05:34.973
Just wait. It's wicked fast
and damn near impossible to see.

01:05:35.181 --> 01:05:37.142
What do I do with it?

01:05:37.350 --> 01:05:40.603
You catch it.
Before the other team's seeker.

01:05:40.854 --> 01:05:43.314
You catch this, the game's over.

01:05:43.523 --> 01:05:47.485
You catch this, Potter,
and we win.

01:05:56.536 --> 01:06:01.875
One of a wizard's most rudimentary
skills is levitation...

01:06:02.083 --> 01:06:06.045
Or the ability to make objects fly.

01:06:06.212 --> 01:06:08.673
Do you have your feathers? Good.

01:06:08.882 --> 01:06:14.053
Now, don't forget the nice wrist
movement we've been practicing.

01:06:14.220 --> 01:06:17.599
The swish and flick. Everyone.

01:06:18.141 --> 01:06:23.730
The swish and flick. Good.
Oh, and enunciate.

01:06:24.481 --> 01:06:28.735
Wingardium leviosa.
Off you go, then.

01:06:29.819 --> 01:06:32.322
Wingardium leviosa.

01:06:32.572 --> 01:06:34.908
Wingardium leviosa.

01:06:35.116 --> 01:06:38.578
Wingardium leviosa.

01:06:38.745 --> 01:06:42.999
No, stop, stop, stop! You're going
to take someone's eye out.

01:06:43.249 --> 01:06:49.214
Besides, you're saying it wrong.
It's leviosa, not leviosar.

01:06:49.756 --> 01:06:54.010
You do it then, if you're so clever.
Go on, go on.

01:06:55.261 --> 01:06:58.348
Wingardium leviosa.

01:07:05.855 --> 01:07:11.444
Well done! See here, everyone,
miss Granger's done it!

01:07:11.694 --> 01:07:13.363
Splendid!

01:07:14.948 --> 01:07:17.116
Well done, dear.

01:07:21.371 --> 01:07:25.458
I think we're going to need
another feather over here.

01:07:31.965 --> 01:07:36.219
"It's leviosa, not leviosar."

01:07:36.469 --> 01:07:41.808
She's a nightmare, honestly!
No wonder she hasn't got any friends.

01:07:42.475 --> 01:07:44.978
I think she heard you.

01:08:13.673 --> 01:08:15.758
Where's Hermione?

01:08:15.967 --> 01:08:19.095
Parvati said she wouldn't
come out of the bathroom.

01:08:19.304 --> 01:08:23.349
She said that she'd been in there
all afternoon, crying.

01:08:27.812 --> 01:08:31.482
Troll in the dungeon!

01:08:31.733 --> 01:08:35.028
Troll in the dungeon!

01:08:37.864 --> 01:08:40.199
Thought you ought to know.

01:08:47.040 --> 01:08:49.876
Silence!

01:08:51.502 --> 01:08:55.548
Everyone will please not panic!

01:08:58.009 --> 01:09:02.555
Prefects will lead their house
back to the dormitories.

01:09:03.264 --> 01:09:08.061
Teachers will follow me
to the dungeons.

01:09:19.072 --> 01:09:22.283
Gryffindors, keep up, please,
and stay alert.

01:09:22.492 --> 01:09:24.243
Harry: How could a troll get in?

01:09:24.410 --> 01:09:29.582
Not on its own. Trolls are really stupid.
Probably people playing jokes.

01:09:29.832 --> 01:09:33.836
- What?
- Hermione! She doesn't know.

01:09:45.932 --> 01:09:49.185
I think the troll's left the dungeon.

01:09:53.064 --> 01:09:55.233
Harry:
It's going into the girls' bathroom.

01:10:26.264 --> 01:10:28.641
Hermione, move!

01:10:31.978 --> 01:10:36.149
Hermione: Help! Help!

01:10:38.151 --> 01:10:40.236
Hey, pea brain!

01:10:52.665 --> 01:10:54.500
Help!

01:11:15.688 --> 01:11:18.024
Do something!

01:11:19.484 --> 01:11:23.446
- What?
- Anything!

01:11:24.030 --> 01:11:26.491
- Hurry up!
- Swish and flick.

01:11:26.699 --> 01:11:29.035
Wingardium leviosa.

01:12:06.364 --> 01:12:09.200
Is it dead?

01:12:09.408 --> 01:12:13.329
I don't think so. Just knocked out.

01:12:18.709 --> 01:12:21.921
Ugh. Troll boogers.

01:12:24.423 --> 01:12:27.969
Oh, my goodness!
Explain yourselves, both of you!

01:12:28.177 --> 01:12:32.765
- Well, what it is...
- It's my fault, professor McGonagall.

01:12:34.976 --> 01:12:36.185
Miss Granger?

01:12:37.061 --> 01:12:42.108
I went looking for the troll.
I thought I could handle it.

01:12:42.358 --> 01:12:44.235
But I was wrong.

01:12:44.443 --> 01:12:49.490
If Harry and Ron hadn't come
and found me, I'd probably be dead.

01:12:50.491 --> 01:12:54.912
McGonagall: Be that as it may,
it was an extremely foolish thing to do.

01:12:55.121 --> 01:13:00.793
I expected more rational behavior
and am very disappointed in you.

01:13:01.002 --> 01:13:04.005
Five points will be taken
from Gryffindor...

01:13:04.213 --> 01:13:07.800
For your serious lack of judgement.

01:13:08.259 --> 01:13:10.261
As for you two gentlemen...

01:13:10.469 --> 01:13:13.890
I just hope you realize
how fortunate you are.

01:13:14.098 --> 01:13:17.518
Not many first-year students
could take on a troll...

01:13:17.727 --> 01:13:20.313
And live to tell the tale.

01:13:20.605 --> 01:13:23.024
Five points...

01:13:24.400 --> 01:13:27.528
Will be awarded to each of you...

01:13:29.113 --> 01:13:32.158
For sheer dumb luck.

01:13:37.788 --> 01:13:41.542
Perhaps you ought to go.
It might wake up.

01:13:49.842 --> 01:13:52.094
Ron:
Take a bit of toast, mate. Go on.

01:13:52.303 --> 01:13:55.514
Ron's right.
You'll need your strength today.

01:13:55.681 --> 01:13:57.934
I'm not hungry.

01:13:58.517 --> 01:14:04.148
Good luck today, Potter.
You've proven yourself against a troll.

01:14:04.357 --> 01:14:07.526
A game of Quidditch
should be easy work.

01:14:07.693 --> 01:14:10.863
Even if it is against Slytherin.

01:14:18.537 --> 01:14:21.958
- That explains the blood.
- Blood?

01:14:22.375 --> 01:14:26.504
Last night, I'm guessing Snape let
the troll in as a diversion...

01:14:26.712 --> 01:14:29.382
So he could get past that dog.

01:14:29.590 --> 01:14:32.343
But he got bit,
that's why he's limping.

01:14:32.593 --> 01:14:34.804
But why would anyone go near that dog?

01:14:35.471 --> 01:14:38.724
At gringotts, Hagrid took
something out of the vault.

01:14:38.891 --> 01:14:42.186
Said it was Hogwarts business,
very secret.

01:14:42.353 --> 01:14:43.521
Hermione: You're saying...

01:14:43.729 --> 01:14:48.234
That's what the dog's guarding.
That's what Snape wants.

01:15:01.372 --> 01:15:05.334
- Bit early for mail, isn't it?
- But I never get mail.

01:15:05.876 --> 01:15:07.420
Let's open it.

01:15:17.596 --> 01:15:18.848
Harry: It's a broomstick.

01:15:19.640 --> 01:15:23.769
That's not just a broomstick,
it's a nimbus 2000!

01:15:25.229 --> 01:15:27.273
But who...?

01:15:48.919 --> 01:15:51.422
- Scared, Harry?
- A little.

01:15:51.630 --> 01:15:55.301
It's all right. I felt the same way
before my first game.

01:15:55.468 --> 01:15:58.971
- What happened?
- I don't really remember.

01:15:59.305 --> 01:16:01.974
I took a bludger to the head
two minutes in.

01:16:02.183 --> 01:16:04.977
Woke up in hospital a week later.

01:16:27.208 --> 01:16:30.586
Welcome to Hogwarts' first
Quidditch game of the season.

01:16:30.795 --> 01:16:35.174
Today's game,
Slytherin versus Gryffindor!

01:16:40.346 --> 01:16:42.181
Gryffindor!

01:17:05.788 --> 01:17:08.249
Lee:
The players take their positions...

01:17:08.457 --> 01:17:12.253
As madam hooch steps onto
the field to begin the game!

01:17:12.461 --> 01:17:15.798
Now, I want a nice, clean game...

01:17:16.382 --> 01:17:18.843
From all of you!

01:17:23.973 --> 01:17:26.892
Lee: The bludgers are up,
followed by the golden snitch.

01:17:27.059 --> 01:17:29.812
Remember, the snitch
is worth 150 points.

01:17:30.020 --> 01:17:33.816
The seeker who catches the snitch
ends the game.

01:17:39.905 --> 01:17:44.076
The quaffle is released
and the game begins!

01:18:02.761 --> 01:18:07.558
Angelina Johnson scores!
Ten points for Gryffindor!

01:18:09.810 --> 01:18:12.062
Yes... whoa.

01:18:18.402 --> 01:18:24.116
Lee: Slytherin takes the quaffle.
Bletchley passes to captain Marcus flint.

01:18:55.439 --> 01:18:58.943
- Yes!
- Another 10 points to Gryffindor!

01:19:12.748 --> 01:19:14.625
Give me that!

01:19:46.031 --> 01:19:48.701
Take that side!

01:20:38.167 --> 01:20:41.420
Hagrid: What's going on
with Harry's broomstick?

01:20:50.346 --> 01:20:52.556
It's Snape.
He's jinxing the broom!

01:20:52.765 --> 01:20:57.102
- Jinxing the broom? What do we do?
- Leave it to me.

01:21:18.916 --> 01:21:20.459
Come on, Hermione!

01:21:34.556 --> 01:21:38.310
Lacarnum lnflamarae.

01:21:45.401 --> 01:21:48.445
Man: Fire! You're on fire!

01:22:06.296 --> 01:22:08.465
Go, go, go, go!

01:23:00.476 --> 01:23:02.811
Looks like he's gonna be sick.

01:23:03.896 --> 01:23:05.355
Lee: He's got the snitch!

01:23:05.564 --> 01:23:09.651
Harry Potter receives 150 points
for catching the snitch!

01:23:09.860 --> 01:23:11.528
Gryffindor wins!

01:23:15.157 --> 01:23:17.659
Oh, no.

01:23:55.197 --> 01:23:59.368
Nonsense! Why would Snape
put a curse on Harry's broom?

01:23:59.576 --> 01:24:03.455
Who knows? Why was he trying
to get past that three-headed dog?

01:24:03.705 --> 01:24:06.124
- Who told you about fluffy?
- —fluffy?

01:24:06.291 --> 01:24:09.962
- That thing has a name?
- Of course he has a name. He's mine.

01:24:10.170 --> 01:24:14.758
I bought him off an irishman.
I lent him to Dumbledore to guard...

01:24:14.925 --> 01:24:15.968
Yes?

01:24:16.176 --> 01:24:20.305
Shouldn't have said that.
No more questions! That's top-secret.

01:24:20.889 --> 01:24:24.893
But whatever fluffy's guarding,
Snape's trying to steal it.

01:24:25.102 --> 01:24:28.564
Codswallop. Professor Snape
is a Hogwarts teacher.

01:24:29.064 --> 01:24:34.152
Teacher or not, I know a spell when
I see one. I've read all about them.

01:24:34.319 --> 01:24:37.948
You've got to keep eye contact,
and Snape wasn't blinking.

01:24:38.156 --> 01:24:40.409
Exactly.

01:24:41.076 --> 01:24:43.829
Now, you listen to me,
all three of you.

01:24:43.996 --> 01:24:48.709
You're meddling in things that ought
not to be meddled in. It's dangerous.

01:24:48.917 --> 01:24:54.006
What that dog is guarding is between
Dumbledore and Nicholas flamel.

01:24:54.214 --> 01:24:55.632
Nicholas flamel?

01:24:56.633 --> 01:25:01.346
I shouldn't have said that.
I should not have said that.

01:25:01.513 --> 01:25:05.642
Nicholas flamel.
Who's Nicholas flamel?

01:25:05.851 --> 01:25:07.853
I don't know.

01:25:26.705 --> 01:25:29.541
Merry Christmas merry Christmas

01:25:29.791 --> 01:25:32.544
ring the hogwart bell

01:25:32.794 --> 01:25:35.547
merry Christmas merry Christmas

01:25:35.797 --> 01:25:38.717
cast 3 Christmas spell

01:25:52.314 --> 01:25:55.651
Knight to e5.

01:26:03.325 --> 01:26:05.494
Queen to e5.

01:26:11.083 --> 01:26:12.542
That's totally barbaric!

01:26:13.168 --> 01:26:16.713
That's wizard's chess.
I see you've packed.

01:26:16.922 --> 01:26:18.382
I see you haven't.

01:26:18.757 --> 01:26:23.887
Change of plans. My parents went
to Romania to visit my brother Charlie.

01:26:24.096 --> 01:26:27.933
- He's studying dragons there.
- Good. You can help Harry.

01:26:28.100 --> 01:26:31.520
He's going to the library
to look up Nicholas flamel.

01:26:31.728 --> 01:26:35.232
We've looked a hundred times!

01:26:35.857 --> 01:26:41.113
Not in the restricted section.
Happy Christmas.

01:26:43.323 --> 01:26:46.243
I think we've had
a bad influence on her.

01:26:48.787 --> 01:26:53.125
Ron: Harry, wake up!
Come on, Harry, wake up!

01:27:02.968 --> 01:27:06.304
- Happy Christmas, Harry.
- Happy Christmas, Ron.

01:27:06.471 --> 01:27:08.724
What are you wearing?

01:27:09.307 --> 01:27:12.978
Oh, my mum made it.
Looks like you've got one too.

01:27:14.146 --> 01:27:16.565
- I've got presents?
- Yeah.

01:27:23.989 --> 01:27:26.074
Ron: There they are.

01:27:37.085 --> 01:27:40.589
"Your father left this
in my possession before he died.

01:27:40.839 --> 01:27:44.968
It is time it was returned to you.
Use it well."

01:28:01.777 --> 01:28:05.489
- What is it?
- Some kind of cloak.

01:28:05.781 --> 01:28:08.700
Well, let's see, then. Put it on.

01:28:14.122 --> 01:28:15.415
My body's gone!

01:28:15.624 --> 01:28:19.211
I know what that is.
That's an invisibility cloak!

01:28:19.711 --> 01:28:21.671
I'm invisible?

01:28:22.130 --> 01:28:26.551
They're really rare.
I wonder who gave it to you.

01:28:27.010 --> 01:28:31.807
There was no name.
It just said, "use it well."

01:28:59.876 --> 01:29:05.757
Famous fire-eaters.
Fifteenth-century fiends.

01:29:05.966 --> 01:29:11.763
Flamel. Nicholas flamel.
Where are you?

01:29:30.615 --> 01:29:32.534
Filch: Who's there?

01:29:38.623 --> 01:29:44.296
I know you're in there.
You can't hide.

01:29:51.636 --> 01:29:55.432
Who is it? Show yourself.

01:30:42.604 --> 01:30:43.980
Quirrell: Severus, I...

01:30:44.648 --> 01:30:48.526
You don't want me
as your enemy, quirrell.

01:30:48.693 --> 01:30:53.448
- I don't know what you mean.
- You know perfectly well what I mean.

01:31:10.674 --> 01:31:13.885
We'll have another little chat soon.

01:31:14.094 --> 01:31:19.557
When you've had time to decide
where your loyalties lie.

01:31:19.808 --> 01:31:24.229
Professors. I found this
in the restricted section.

01:31:24.729 --> 01:31:29.818
It's still hot. That means
there's a student out of bed.

01:33:01.910 --> 01:33:03.745
Mum?

01:33:06.998 --> 01:33:09.000
Dad?

01:33:43.743 --> 01:33:48.706
Harry: Ron, you've really gotta
see this! Ron, you've gotta see this!

01:33:50.542 --> 01:33:53.378
Ron, come on, get out of bed!

01:33:53.628 --> 01:33:57.215
- —Why?- There's something you've got to see!

01:34:03.888 --> 01:34:08.226
Come on! Come!
Come look, it's my parents!

01:34:09.686 --> 01:34:11.646
I only see us.

01:34:11.896 --> 01:34:15.233
Look in properly.
Go on, stand there.

01:34:15.400 --> 01:34:21.364
- There. You see them, don't you?
- That's me! Only I'm head boy.

01:34:21.865 --> 01:34:24.200
And I'm holding the Quidditch cup.

01:34:24.409 --> 01:34:28.580
And bloody hell!
I'm Quidditch captain too!

01:34:29.747 --> 01:34:32.208
I look good.

01:34:32.834 --> 01:34:36.671
Harry, do you think this mirror
shows the future?

01:34:36.880 --> 01:34:41.843
How can it?
Both my parents are dead.

01:35:04.949 --> 01:35:07.118
Back again, Harry?

01:35:10.246 --> 01:35:12.749
I see that you,
like many before you...

01:35:12.957 --> 01:35:17.128
Have discovered the delights
of the mirror of erised.

01:35:17.462 --> 01:35:21.633
I trust by now
you realize what it does.

01:35:22.926 --> 01:35:25.470
Let me give you a clue.

01:35:25.970 --> 01:35:28.139
The happiest man on earth...

01:35:28.348 --> 01:35:31.726
Would look in the mirror
and see only himself...

01:35:31.935 --> 01:35:34.270
Exactly as he is.

01:35:34.479 --> 01:35:39.484
So then, it shows us what we want.
Whatever we want.

01:35:43.488 --> 01:35:45.990
It shows us nothing more or less...

01:35:46.157 --> 01:35:52.163
Than the deepest and most desperate
desires of our hearts.

01:35:52.372 --> 01:35:57.085
Now you, Harry, who have
never known your family...

01:35:57.293 --> 01:36:01.172
You see them standing beside you.

01:36:01.381 --> 01:36:03.800
But remember this, Harry.

01:36:04.008 --> 01:36:09.931
This mirror gives us
neither knowledge...

01:36:10.139 --> 01:36:12.267
Or truth.

01:36:13.184 --> 01:36:19.274
Men have wasted away in front of it.
Even gone mad.

01:36:20.316 --> 01:36:24.445
That is why tomorrow
it will be moved to a new home.

01:36:24.654 --> 01:36:26.531
And I must ask you...

01:36:27.532 --> 01:36:31.411
Not to go looking for it again.

01:36:32.161 --> 01:36:35.290
It does not do to dwell on dreams...

01:36:35.873 --> 01:36:38.710
And forget to live.

01:37:34.223 --> 01:37:39.103
I had you looking in the wrong section.
How could I be so stupid?

01:37:39.395 --> 01:37:42.482
I checked this out weeks ago
for a bit of light reading.

01:37:42.690 --> 01:37:44.692
This is light?

01:37:49.280 --> 01:37:51.699
Of course! Here it is!

01:37:51.908 --> 01:37:55.912
Nicholas flamel is the only known
maker of the philosopher's stone.

01:37:56.120 --> 01:37:57.288
The what?

01:37:57.997 --> 01:38:01.000
Honestly, don't you two read?

01:38:01.209 --> 01:38:05.713
"The philosopher's stone is a legendary
substance with astonishing powers.

01:38:05.922 --> 01:38:08.549
It'll transform any metal
into pure gold...

01:38:08.758 --> 01:38:12.762
And produces the elixir of life
which will make the drinker immortal."

01:38:12.970 --> 01:38:15.139
- Immortal?
- It means you'll never die.

01:38:15.306 --> 01:38:17.433
I know what it means!

01:38:18.309 --> 01:38:23.022
"The only stone currently in existence
belongs to Mr. Nicholas flamel...

01:38:23.231 --> 01:38:28.403
The noted alchemist who last year
celebrated his 665th birthday."

01:38:30.113 --> 01:38:32.281
That's what fluffy's guarding.

01:38:32.490 --> 01:38:37.161
That's what's under the trap door.
The philosopher's stone.

01:38:53.970 --> 01:38:57.765
Don't wish to be rude,
but I'm in no state to entertain.

01:38:57.974 --> 01:39:00.685
All:
We know about the philosopher's stone.

01:39:05.356 --> 01:39:10.528
- We think Snape's trying to steal it.
- Are you still on about him?

01:39:10.695 --> 01:39:13.531
We know he's after it.
We don't know why.

01:39:13.865 --> 01:39:18.077
Snape is one of the teachers
protecting the stone. He won't steal it.

01:39:18.327 --> 01:39:19.370
What?

01:39:19.579 --> 01:39:22.999
You heard. Come on,
I'm a bit preoccupied today.

01:39:23.207 --> 01:39:25.877
Harry: Wait a minute.
"One of the teachers"?

01:39:26.085 --> 01:39:29.964
There are other things
defending the stone, aren't there?

01:39:30.173 --> 01:39:32.800
- Spells, enchantments.
- Hagrid: Right.

01:39:33.050 --> 01:39:36.095
Waste of bloody time, if you ask me.

01:39:36.304 --> 01:39:38.389
Ain't no one gonna get past fluffy.

01:39:38.598 --> 01:39:42.226
Ain't a soul knows how,
except for me and Dumbledore.

01:39:42.518 --> 01:39:46.063
I shouldn't have told you that.
I should not have told you that.

01:39:59.911 --> 01:40:05.041
- Hagrid, what exactly is that?
- That? It's...

01:40:05.249 --> 01:40:07.251
I know what that is!

01:40:07.502 --> 01:40:10.129
But, Hagrid, how did you get one?

01:40:10.505 --> 01:40:13.758
I won it. Off a stranger
I met down at the pub.

01:40:13.925 --> 01:40:18.054
Seemed quite glad to be rid of it,
as a matter of fact.

01:40:43.287 --> 01:40:44.455
A dragon?

01:40:44.664 --> 01:40:49.085
That's not just a dragon.
That's a Norwegian ridgeback.

01:40:49.293 --> 01:40:52.171
My brother works
with these in Romania.

01:40:52.380 --> 01:40:57.260
Isn't he beautiful? Oh, bless him.
Look, he knows his mummy.

01:40:57.927 --> 01:40:59.679
Hello, norbert.

01:40:59.971 --> 01:41:04.308
- Norbert?
- He's gotta have a name, don't he?

01:41:05.059 --> 01:41:07.478
Don't you, norbert?

01:41:14.485 --> 01:41:17.613
He'll have to be trained up a bit,
of course.

01:41:21.492 --> 01:41:23.578
Who's that?

01:41:25.288 --> 01:41:27.331
Malfoy.

01:41:28.124 --> 01:41:29.500
Oh, dear.

01:41:31.252 --> 01:41:36.007
Harry: Hagrid always wanted a dragon.
Told me so the first time I met him.

01:41:36.257 --> 01:41:40.303
Ron: It's crazy.
And worse, Malfoy knows.

01:41:40.511 --> 01:41:44.599
- Harry: I don't understand. Is that bad?
- It's bad.

01:41:44.849 --> 01:41:47.018
Good evening.

01:41:50.688 --> 01:41:53.608
Nothing, I repeat, nothing...

01:41:53.858 --> 01:41:57.361
Gives a student the right
to walk about at night.

01:41:57.528 --> 01:42:02.450
Therefore, as punishment for your
actions, 50 points will be taken.

01:42:06.037 --> 01:42:08.372
To ensure it doesn't happen again...

01:42:08.623 --> 01:42:11.959
All four of you
will receive detention.

01:42:12.877 --> 01:42:15.838
Excuse me, professor,
perhaps I heard you wrong.

01:42:16.047 --> 01:42:18.382
I thought you said the four of us.

01:42:18.549 --> 01:42:21.052
No, you heard me correctly.

01:42:21.302 --> 01:42:26.307
Honorable as your intentions were,
you too were out of bed after hours.

01:42:26.766 --> 01:42:29.727
You will join your classmates
in detention.

01:42:40.905 --> 01:42:44.909
Filch: A pity they let
the old punishments die.

01:42:45.159 --> 01:42:49.872
Was a time detention found you
hanging by your thumbs in the dungeons.

01:42:50.081 --> 01:42:52.917
God, I miss the screaming.

01:42:55.419 --> 01:42:58.756
You'll be serving detention
with Hagrid tonight.

01:42:58.923 --> 01:43:04.303
He's got a little job to do
inside the dark forest.

01:43:06.389 --> 01:43:09.350
A sorry lot, this, Hagrid.

01:43:10.810 --> 01:43:15.815
Good god, you're not still on
about that bloody dragon, are you?

01:43:18.067 --> 01:43:20.111
Norbert's gone.

01:43:20.695 --> 01:43:24.240
Dumbledore sent him off to Romania
to live in a colony.

01:43:24.532 --> 01:43:27.785
That's good, isn't it?
He's with his own kind.

01:43:27.952 --> 01:43:30.287
What if he don't like Romania?

01:43:30.454 --> 01:43:34.750
What if the other dragons are mean
to him? He's only a baby.

01:43:35.376 --> 01:43:40.631
For god's sake, pull yourself together.
You're going into the forest.

01:43:40.840 --> 01:43:43.217
Got to have your wits about you.

01:43:43.426 --> 01:43:49.098
The forest? I thought that was a joke.
We can't go in there.

01:43:49.557 --> 01:43:53.144
Students aren't allowed.
And there are...

01:43:54.937 --> 01:43:56.147
Werewolves.

01:43:56.605 --> 01:43:59.900
There's more than werewolves
in those trees.

01:44:00.109 --> 01:44:02.778
You can be sure of that.

01:44:04.739 --> 01:44:06.157
Nighty-night.

01:44:08.743 --> 01:44:11.579
Right. Let's go.

01:44:49.784 --> 01:44:52.203
Hagrid, what is that?

01:44:52.411 --> 01:44:55.790
What we're here for. See that?

01:44:56.290 --> 01:45:01.670
That's unicorn blood, that is.
I found one dead a few weeks ago.

01:45:02.213 --> 01:45:06.801
Now, this one's been hurt bad
by something.

01:45:14.308 --> 01:45:20.064
So, it's ourjob to go
and find the poor beast.

01:45:20.231 --> 01:45:23.400
- Ron, Hermione, come with me.
- Okay.

01:45:23.859 --> 01:45:27.154
And, Harry, you'll go with Malfoy.

01:45:28.405 --> 01:45:30.699
Okay. Then I get fang.

01:45:30.866 --> 01:45:36.580
Fine. Just so you know,
he's a bloody coward.

01:45:40.251 --> 01:45:45.256
Wait till my father hears
about this. This is servant's stuff.

01:45:45.506 --> 01:45:49.426
If I didn't know better,
I'd say you were scared.

01:45:49.593 --> 01:45:51.929
I'm not scared, Potter.

01:45:53.347 --> 01:45:55.266
Do you hear that?

01:45:57.852 --> 01:45:59.270
Come on, fang.

01:45:59.478 --> 01:46:00.980
Scared!

01:46:25.963 --> 01:46:28.132
What is it, fang?

01:47:38.494 --> 01:47:43.999
Harry Potter, you must leave.
You are known to many creatures here.

01:47:44.208 --> 01:47:48.212
The forest is not safe at this time.
Especially for you.

01:47:48.379 --> 01:47:51.173
What was that thing you saved me from?

01:47:51.382 --> 01:47:56.720
A monstrous creature.
It is a terrible crime to slay a unicorn.

01:47:56.887 --> 01:48:02.476
Drinking its blood will keep you alive
even if you are an inch from death.

01:48:02.685 --> 01:48:07.731
But at a terrible price. For you
have slain something so pure...

01:48:07.982 --> 01:48:12.820
That the moment the blood touches
your lips, you will have a half-life.

01:48:13.028 --> 01:48:14.822
A cursed life.

01:48:15.030 --> 01:48:18.993
- Who would choose such a life?
- Can you think of no one?

01:48:19.201 --> 01:48:24.164
Do you mean to say that
that thing that killed the unicorn...

01:48:24.498 --> 01:48:28.419
That was drinking its blood,
that was Voldemort?

01:48:28.627 --> 01:48:33.757
Do you know what is hidden
in the school at this very moment?

01:48:34.633 --> 01:48:36.176
The philosopher's stone.

01:48:37.594 --> 01:48:39.513
Harry!

01:48:40.097 --> 01:48:44.601
Hello there, firenze.
See you've met our young Mr. Potter.

01:48:44.768 --> 01:48:46.937
You all right there, Harry?

01:48:48.105 --> 01:48:52.401
Harry Potter,
this is where I leave you.

01:48:53.277 --> 01:48:57.114
You're safe now. Good luck.

01:49:04.747 --> 01:49:08.876
Hermione: You mean, you-know-who
is out there right now in the forest?

01:49:09.084 --> 01:49:11.879
But he's weak.
He's living off the unicorns.

01:49:12.087 --> 01:49:14.965
Don't you see? We had it wrong.

01:49:15.215 --> 01:49:19.595
Snape doesn't want the stone
for himself. He wants it for Voldemort.

01:49:19.803 --> 01:49:24.308
With the elixir of life,
Voldemort will be strong again.

01:49:24.558 --> 01:49:26.143
He'll come back.

01:49:26.310 --> 01:49:28.103
Ron: But if he comes back...

01:49:28.312 --> 01:49:32.316
You don't think he'll try
to kill you, do you?

01:49:33.317 --> 01:49:36.820
If he'd had the chance,
he might have tried tonight.

01:49:37.071 --> 01:49:40.657
And to think I've been worrying
about my potions final.

01:49:40.824 --> 01:49:44.453
Hermione: Hang on a minute.
We're forgetting one thing.

01:49:44.828 --> 01:49:49.708
Who's the one wizard
Voldemort always feared?

01:49:50.459 --> 01:49:55.589
Dumbledore. As long as Dumbledore
is around, Harry, you're safe.

01:49:55.798 --> 01:49:59.843
As long as Dumbledore is around,
you can't be touched.

01:50:05.599 --> 01:50:11.021
Hermione: I'd heard Hogwarts' final
exams were frightful, but that was fun.

01:50:11.230 --> 01:50:14.858
Speak for yourself.
All right there, Harry?

01:50:15.109 --> 01:50:20.280
- My scar. It keeps burning.
- It's happened before.

01:50:20.489 --> 01:50:23.158
- Not like this.
- Ron: You should see the nurse.

01:50:23.367 --> 01:50:26.870
Harry: I think it's a warning.
It means danger's coming.

01:50:34.503 --> 01:50:36.964
- Of course!
- What is it?

01:50:37.172 --> 01:50:40.884
Isn't it odd that what Hagrid wants
more than anything is a dragon...

01:50:41.135 --> 01:50:44.221
And a strangerjust happens
to have one?

01:50:44.388 --> 01:50:47.057
How many people wander around
with dragon eggs?

01:50:47.307 --> 01:50:49.560
Why didn't I see it before?

01:50:55.149 --> 01:50:58.652
Who gave you the egg?
What did he look like?

01:50:58.861 --> 01:51:01.572
I never saw his face.
He kept his hood up.

01:51:01.822 --> 01:51:04.408
You and this stranger
must have talked.

01:51:04.992 --> 01:51:08.537
He wanted to know what sort
of creatures I looked after.

01:51:08.745 --> 01:51:12.749
I said, "after fluffy,
a dragon's gonna be no problem."

01:51:12.916 --> 01:51:17.421
- Was he interested in fluffy?
- Of course he was interested.

01:51:17.838 --> 01:51:22.009
How often do you come across
a three-headed dog?

01:51:22.217 --> 01:51:27.848
But I told him, "the trick with any beast
is to know how to calm him."

01:51:28.056 --> 01:51:33.520
Take fluffy, for example. Play him
music and he falls straight to sleep.

01:51:35.105 --> 01:51:37.858
I shouldn't have told you that.

01:51:38.108 --> 01:51:40.319
Where are you going?

01:51:47.326 --> 01:51:50.078
We have to see Dumbledore.
Immediately!

01:51:50.537 --> 01:51:53.123
I'm afraid he's not here.

01:51:53.373 --> 01:51:57.628
He received an urgent owl
from the ministry of magic and left.

01:51:58.086 --> 01:52:03.175
He's gone? But this is important!
This is about the philosopher's stone!

01:52:04.968 --> 01:52:08.722
- How do you know...?
- Someone's going to try and steal it.

01:52:09.348 --> 01:52:14.561
I don't know how you know,
but I assure you it is well protected.

01:52:14.770 --> 01:52:19.066
Now would you go back
to your dormitories? Quietly.

01:52:27.366 --> 01:52:30.160
That was no stranger Hagrid met.
It was Snape.

01:52:30.369 --> 01:52:32.996
Which means he knows
how to get past fluffy.

01:52:33.247 --> 01:52:37.125
- And with Dumbledore gone...
- Good afternoon.

01:52:39.169 --> 01:52:42.256
What would three young Gryffindors...

01:52:42.506 --> 01:52:46.802
Be doing inside on a day like this?

01:52:51.515 --> 01:52:55.102
- We were just...
- You ought to be careful.

01:52:55.644 --> 01:52:57.604
People will think you're...

01:53:01.900 --> 01:53:04.611
Up to something.

01:53:14.913 --> 01:53:16.915
Now what do we do?

01:53:17.124 --> 01:53:20.877
We go down the trap door. Tonight.

01:53:34.641 --> 01:53:36.059
Harry: Trevor.

01:53:36.435 --> 01:53:39.855
Trevor, go! You shouldn't be here!

01:53:40.063 --> 01:53:45.527
Neither should you.
You're sneaking out again, aren't you?

01:53:45.736 --> 01:53:49.698
- Neville, listen. We were...
- No, I won't let you!

01:53:49.948 --> 01:53:54.536
You'll get Gryffindor into trouble again.
Phfightyou.

01:53:54.745 --> 01:53:59.041
Neville, I'm really sorry about this.
Petrificus totalus.

01:54:07.007 --> 01:54:10.761
You're a little scary sometimes,
you know that?

01:54:11.053 --> 01:54:14.681
Brilliant, but scary.

01:54:15.349 --> 01:54:17.392
Let's go.

01:54:17.601 --> 01:54:21.855
Hermione: Sorry.
Ron: It's for your own good, you know.

01:54:27.277 --> 01:54:31.239
- You stood on my foot!
- Sorry.

01:54:35.118 --> 01:54:37.120
Hermione: Alohomora.

01:54:49.132 --> 01:54:51.760
Harry: Wait a minute. He's...

01:54:52.969 --> 01:54:55.138
."Snonng.

01:54:57.641 --> 01:55:03.146
Harry: Snape's already been here.
He's put a spell on the harp.

01:55:04.773 --> 01:55:07.776
Ron: It's got horrible breath.

01:55:10.320 --> 01:55:12.447
- Harry: We have to move its paw.
- What?

01:55:12.656 --> 01:55:14.074
Come on!

01:55:18.120 --> 01:55:20.163
Okay. Push.

01:55:43.353 --> 01:55:46.982
I'll go first. Don't follow
until I give you a sign.

01:55:47.190 --> 01:55:52.195
If something bad happens,
get yourselves out.

01:55:52.988 --> 01:55:56.450
Does it seem a bit quiet to you?

01:55:57.159 --> 01:55:58.994
The harp.

01:55:59.661 --> 01:56:02.372
It's stopped playing.

01:56:03.790 --> 01:56:08.170
Ugh. Yuck!

01:56:12.382 --> 01:56:13.550
Harry: Jump!

01:56:27.731 --> 01:56:31.359
Lucky this plant thing's here, really.

01:56:45.749 --> 01:56:48.877
Hermione: Stop moving, both of you.
This is devil's snare.

01:56:49.085 --> 01:56:52.756
You have to relax. If you don't,
it will only kill you faster.

01:56:53.006 --> 01:56:58.011
Kill us faster?
Oh, now I can relax!

01:57:00.263 --> 01:57:01.598
Hermione!

01:57:02.182 --> 01:57:05.936
- Now what are we gonna do?
- Hermione: Just relax!

01:57:06.186 --> 01:57:10.690
- Hermione, where are you?
- Do what I say! Trust me.

01:57:14.569 --> 01:57:16.696
Harry!

01:57:17.781 --> 01:57:21.117
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

01:57:21.284 --> 01:57:24.371
- He's not relaxing, is he?
- Apparently not.

01:57:24.579 --> 01:57:27.123
- We've gotta do something.
- What?

01:57:27.290 --> 01:57:30.252
I remember reading something
in herbology.

01:57:31.127 --> 01:57:34.965
Devil's snare, devil's snare.
It's deadly fun...

01:57:35.173 --> 01:57:39.553
But will sulk in the sun!
That's it! It hates sunlight.

01:57:39.803 --> 01:57:41.805
Lumus solem.

01:57:49.938 --> 01:57:52.482
- Ron, you okay?
- Yeah.

01:57:55.235 --> 01:57:57.696
Lucky we didn't panic.

01:57:58.446 --> 01:58:01.950
Lucky Hermione pays attention
in herbology.

01:58:03.577 --> 01:58:05.078
Hermione: What is that?

01:58:05.287 --> 01:58:08.957
I don't know. Sounds like wings.

01:58:22.137 --> 01:58:25.599
Hermione: Curious.
I've never seen birds like these.

01:58:25.807 --> 01:58:29.436
Harry: They're not birds.
They're keys.

01:58:29.644 --> 01:58:33.106
And I'll bet one of them
fits that door.

01:58:36.526 --> 01:58:41.197
- What's this all about?
- I don't know.

01:58:47.037 --> 01:58:49.122
Strange.
01:58:49.539 --> 01:58:51.833
Ron: Alohomora!

01:58:54.794 --> 01:58:57.047
Well, it was worth a try.

01:58:57.255 --> 01:59:00.508
What will we do?
There must be a thousand keys.

01:59:00.717 --> 01:59:04.638
Ron: We want a big, old-fashioned one.
Probably rusty.

01:59:04.846 --> 01:59:08.266
I see it!
The one with the broken wing.

01:59:11.853 --> 01:59:14.189
What's wrong?

01:59:15.065 --> 01:59:16.566
It's too simple.

01:59:16.775 --> 01:59:21.529
Go on! If Snape could catch it
on that old broomstick, you can.

01:59:21.738 --> 01:59:25.283
You're the youngest seeker
in a century.

01:59:42.092 --> 01:59:45.095
This complicates things a bit.

02:00:06.408 --> 02:00:08.326
Harry: Catch the key!

02:00:12.747 --> 02:00:14.624
Hurry up!

02:00:47.157 --> 02:00:51.828
Hermione: I don't like this.
I don't like this at all.

02:00:51.995 --> 02:00:55.165
Where are we? A graveyard.

02:00:55.582 --> 02:00:58.168
This is no graveyard.

02:01:05.675 --> 02:01:08.636
It's a chessboard.

02:01:20.607 --> 02:01:22.525
There's the door.

02:01:34.537 --> 02:01:36.039
Now what do we do?

02:01:36.456 --> 02:01:40.543
It's obvious, isn't it? We've got
to play our way across the room.

02:01:41.169 --> 02:01:44.923
Harry, you take
the empty bishop's square.

02:01:45.215 --> 02:01:49.469
Hermione, you'll be
the queen-side castle.

02:01:49.719 --> 02:01:53.723
As for me, I'll be a knight.

02:02:00.939 --> 02:02:02.649
What happens now?

02:02:03.441 --> 02:02:06.444
Well, white moves first.

02:02:10.240 --> 02:02:11.533
We play.

02:02:22.085 --> 02:02:27.173
Ron, you don't suppose
this is going to be like...

02:02:27.423 --> 02:02:30.969
Real wizard's chess, do you?

02:02:31.344 --> 02:02:34.264
You there, d5.

02:02:48.903 --> 02:02:50.488
Yes, Hermione.

02:02:50.697 --> 02:02:55.785
I think this is gonna be
exactly like wizard's chess.

02:03:01.708 --> 02:03:04.210
Castle to e4!

02:03:07.797 --> 02:03:10.133
Pawn to c3!

02:03:54.761 --> 02:03:58.765
- Wait a minute.
- Ron: You understand right, Harry.

02:03:59.015 --> 02:04:03.686
Once I make my move,
the queen will take me.

02:04:04.354 --> 02:04:06.689
Then you're free to check the king.

02:04:06.856 --> 02:04:09.609
- No. Ron, no!
- What is it?

02:04:10.193 --> 02:04:14.864
- He's going to sacrifice himself.
- No, there must be another way!

02:04:15.114 --> 02:04:18.868
Do you wanna stop Snape
from getting that stone or not?

02:04:19.077 --> 02:04:22.664
Harry, it's you that has to go on.
I know it.

02:04:23.164 --> 02:04:25.875
Not me. Not Hermione. You.

02:04:36.177 --> 02:04:39.097
Knight to h3.

02:05:00.034 --> 02:05:02.036
Check.

02:05:33.192 --> 02:05:38.948
No, don't move!
Don't forget, we're still playing.

02:05:54.047 --> 02:05:55.298
Checkmate.

02:06:15.276 --> 02:06:17.779
Take care of Ron.
Then go to the owlery.

02:06:17.987 --> 02:06:21.824
Send a message to Dumbledore.
Ron's right.

02:06:22.075 --> 02:06:23.951
I have to go on.

02:06:24.452 --> 02:06:30.333
You'll be okay, Harry.
You're a great wizard. You really are.

02:06:30.583 --> 02:06:33.086
Not as good as you.

02:06:33.920 --> 02:06:38.758
Me? Books and cleverness.
There are more important things.

02:06:39.967 --> 02:06:45.598
Friendship and bravery.
And, Harry, just be careful.

02:07:23.678 --> 02:07:25.346
You?

02:07:26.139 --> 02:07:29.976
No, it can't be.
Snape, he was the...

02:07:30.184 --> 02:07:33.229
Quirrell: Yes, he does seem the type,
doesn't he?

02:07:33.396 --> 02:07:36.566
Next to him, who would suspect...

02:07:36.774 --> 02:07:40.695
Poor, stuttering
professor quirrell?

02:07:40.903 --> 02:07:46.284
But that day, during the Quidditch
match, Snape tried to kill me.

02:07:46.492 --> 02:07:49.287
No, dear boy. I tried to kill you!

02:07:49.787 --> 02:07:53.916
If Snape's cloak hadn't caught
fire and broken my eye contact...

02:07:54.167 --> 02:07:56.377
I would have succeeded.

02:07:56.586 --> 02:07:59.589
Even with Snape muttering
his countercurse.

02:07:59.797 --> 02:08:02.008
Snape was trying to save me?

02:08:02.216 --> 02:08:07.555
I knew you were a danger to me,
especially after Halloween.

02:08:07.763 --> 02:08:12.018
- Then you let the troll in!
- Very good, Potter, yes.

02:08:12.226 --> 02:08:15.229
Snape, unfortunately, wasn't fooled.

02:08:15.813 --> 02:08:20.776
While everyone ran about, he went
to the third floor to head me off.

02:08:21.694 --> 02:08:25.198
He, of course, never trusted me again.

02:08:26.199 --> 02:08:31.454
He rarely left me alone.
But he doesn't understand.

02:08:31.621 --> 02:08:35.708
I'm never alone. Never.

02:08:35.917 --> 02:08:39.962
Now, what does this mirror do?

02:08:41.589 --> 02:08:43.716
I see what I desire.

02:08:44.258 --> 02:08:48.638
I see myself holding the stone.
But how do I get it?

02:08:48.888 --> 02:08:51.057
Man: Use the boy.

02:08:51.849 --> 02:08:55.770
Come here, Potter! Now!

02:09:07.865 --> 02:09:11.869
Tell me, what do you see?

02:09:37.019 --> 02:09:39.438
What is it? What do you see?

02:09:39.647 --> 02:09:44.819
I'm shaking hands with Dumbledore.
I've won the house cup.

02:09:45.027 --> 02:09:46.529
Man: He lies.

02:09:47.029 --> 02:09:50.783
Tell the truth! What do you see?

02:09:50.992 --> 02:09:55.371
- Man: Let me speak to him.
- Master, you are not strong enough.

02:09:55.621 --> 02:09:59.625
Man:
I have strength enough for this.

02:10:17.810 --> 02:10:20.688
Harry Potter...

02:10:20.896 --> 02:10:23.232
We meet again.

02:10:23.441 --> 02:10:24.859
Voldemort.

02:10:25.067 --> 02:10:29.030
Yes. You see what I've become?

02:10:29.238 --> 02:10:32.867
See what I must do to survive?

02:10:33.075 --> 02:10:37.204
Live off another. A mere parasite.

02:10:37.872 --> 02:10:41.208
Unicorn blood can sustain me...

02:10:41.417 --> 02:10:45.087
But it cannot give me
a body of my own.

02:10:45.254 --> 02:10:48.841
But there is something that can.

02:10:49.050 --> 02:10:54.722
Something that, conveniently enough,
lies in your pocket.

02:10:55.097 --> 02:10:56.599
Stop him!

02:11:01.687 --> 02:11:04.440
Voldemort: Don't be a fool.

02:11:04.940 --> 02:11:08.069
Why suffer an horrific death...

02:11:08.277 --> 02:11:11.906
When you can join me and live?

02:11:12.114 --> 02:11:13.199
Never!

02:11:15.201 --> 02:11:19.997
Bravery. Your parents had it too.

02:11:20.748 --> 02:11:24.043
Tell me, Harry...

02:11:24.293 --> 02:11:28.130
Would you like to see
your mother and father again?

02:11:28.422 --> 02:11:30.508
Together...

02:11:30.716 --> 02:11:33.260
We can bring them back.

02:11:33.636 --> 02:11:38.391
All I ask is for something in return.

02:11:45.106 --> 02:11:48.234
That's it, Harry.

02:11:49.110 --> 02:11:52.988
There is no good and evil.

02:11:53.155 --> 02:11:56.158
There is only power...

02:11:56.409 --> 02:12:00.538
And those too weak to seek it.

02:12:01.163 --> 02:12:06.252
Together, we'll do
extraordinary things.

02:12:06.669 --> 02:12:08.921
Just give me the stone!

02:12:11.549 --> 02:12:12.675
You liar!

02:12:38.576 --> 02:12:43.873
- What is this magic?
- Fool, get the stone!

02:14:29.186 --> 02:14:31.689
Good afternoon, Harry.

02:14:33.816 --> 02:14:38.320
- Tokens from your admirers?
- Admirers?

02:14:38.487 --> 02:14:44.493
What happened in the dungeons between
you and professor quirrell is a secret.

02:14:44.743 --> 02:14:49.498
So, naturally, the whole school knows.

02:14:51.834 --> 02:14:55.504
I see that your friend Ronald
has saved you the trouble...

02:14:55.713 --> 02:14:58.507
Of opening your chocolate frogs.

02:14:58.757 --> 02:15:01.760
Ron was here? Is he all right?
What about Hermione?

02:15:01.969 --> 02:15:06.849
Fine. They're both just fine.

02:15:07.433 --> 02:15:10.227
- What happened to the stone?
- Relax, dear boy.

02:15:10.519 --> 02:15:13.355
The stone has been destroyed.

02:15:13.647 --> 02:15:17.860
My friend Nicholas and I
have had a little chat...

02:15:18.027 --> 02:15:22.031
And agreed it was best all around.

02:15:22.239 --> 02:15:26.035
But then, flamel,
he'll die, won't he?

02:15:28.120 --> 02:15:33.626
He has enough elixir
to set his affairs in order.

02:15:33.834 --> 02:15:37.046
But yes, he will die.

02:15:37.254 --> 02:15:39.715
How is it I got the stone, sir?

02:15:39.882 --> 02:15:42.468
One minute I was staring
in the mirror and...

02:15:42.676 --> 02:15:46.764
You see, only a person...

02:15:47.056 --> 02:15:50.976
Who wanted to find the stone,
find it...

02:15:51.226 --> 02:15:55.773
But not use it,
would be able to get it.

02:15:56.732 --> 02:16:00.235
That is one of my more brilliant ideas.

02:16:00.402 --> 02:16:05.491
And between you and me,
that is saying something.

02:16:06.909 --> 02:16:12.164
Does that mean, with the stone gone,
that Voldemort can never come back?

02:16:12.373 --> 02:16:14.708
I'm afraid...

02:16:16.085 --> 02:16:20.172
There are ways
in which he can return.

02:16:20.881 --> 02:16:23.425
Harry, do you know why...

02:16:23.676 --> 02:16:27.680
Professor quirrell couldn't bear
to have you touch him?

02:16:27.888 --> 02:16:32.518
It was because of your mother.
She sacrificed herself for you.

02:16:33.060 --> 02:16:36.271
And that kind of act leaves a Mark.

02:16:36.438 --> 02:16:40.275
No, this kind of Mark cannot be seen.

02:16:40.442 --> 02:16:45.406
- It lives in your very skin.
- What is it?

02:16:46.240 --> 02:16:49.952
Love, Harry. Love.

02:16:58.043 --> 02:17:02.131
Bertie bott's every flavor beans.

02:17:02.381 --> 02:17:07.052
I was most unfortunate in my youth
to come across a vomit-flavored one.

02:17:07.302 --> 02:17:10.597
And since then,
I've lost my liking for them.

02:17:10.806 --> 02:17:14.143
But I think I could be safe...

02:17:14.393 --> 02:17:16.770
With a nice toffee.

02:17:19.481 --> 02:17:22.401
Hm, alas!

02:17:23.110 --> 02:17:25.237
Eannax.

02:17:40.461 --> 02:17:43.630
- All right there, Ron?
- All right. You?

02:17:44.757 --> 02:17:47.468
All right. Hermione?

02:17:48.135 --> 02:17:49.970
Never better.

02:18:05.778 --> 02:18:08.197
Another year gone.

02:18:08.989 --> 02:18:13.535
And now, as I understand it,
the house cup needs awarding.

02:18:13.702 --> 02:18:16.371
And the points stand thus:

02:18:16.538 --> 02:18:22.377
In fourth place,
Gryffindor with 312 points.

02:18:24.338 --> 02:18:30.010
Third place,
hufflepuff with 352 points.

02:18:35.307 --> 02:18:37.059
In second place...

02:18:37.309 --> 02:18:42.064
Ravenclaw with 426 points.

02:18:47.736 --> 02:18:49.488
And in first place...

02:18:49.822 --> 02:18:55.244
With 472 points, Slytherin house.

02:19:00.833 --> 02:19:03.043
Nice one, mate.

02:19:06.880 --> 02:19:10.968
Yes, well done, Slytherin.
Well done.

02:19:11.218 --> 02:19:15.514
However, recent events must
be taken into account.

02:19:15.722 --> 02:19:20.686
And I have a few last-minute points
to award.

02:19:21.270 --> 02:19:26.775
To miss Hermione Granger,
for the cool use of intellect...

02:19:27.025 --> 02:19:29.778
While others were in grave peril...

02:19:30.529 --> 02:19:32.781
50 points.

02:19:33.699 --> 02:19:34.992
Good job.

02:19:42.708 --> 02:19:48.755
Second, to Mr. Ronald Weasley,
for the best-played game of chess...

02:19:49.256 --> 02:19:54.511
That Hogwarts has seen
these many years, 50 points.

02:20:01.727 --> 02:20:04.605
To Mr. Harry Potter...

02:20:04.813 --> 02:20:09.109
For pure nerve
and outstanding courage...

02:20:09.651 --> 02:20:14.573
I award Gryffindor house 60 points.

02:20:22.831 --> 02:20:24.791
We're tied with Slytherin!

02:20:25.000 --> 02:20:31.006
Finally, it takes a great deal of bravery
to stand up to your enemies...

02:20:31.173 --> 02:20:35.093
But a great deal more
to stand up to your friends.

02:20:35.302 --> 02:20:38.263
I award 10 points...

02:20:38.472 --> 02:20:41.683
To Neville Longbottom.

02:20:55.030 --> 02:20:58.450
Assuming that my calculations
are correct...

02:20:58.659 --> 02:21:03.205
I believe that a change
of decoration is in order.

02:21:08.210 --> 02:21:11.630
Gryffindor wins the house cup.

02:21:31.316 --> 02:21:32.901
We won!

02:21:49.668 --> 02:21:53.005
Hagrid: Come on, now.
Hurry up, you'll be late.

02:21:53.213 --> 02:21:57.509
Train's leaving. Go on.
Come on, hurry up.

02:22:02.931 --> 02:22:06.226
- Come on, Harry.
- One minute.

02:22:12.441 --> 02:22:16.236
Thought you were leaving
without saying goodbye, did you?

02:22:19.448 --> 02:22:21.283
This is for you.

02:22:38.050 --> 02:22:40.177
Thanks, Hagrid.

02:22:45.974 --> 02:22:50.437
Go on. On with you. On with you now.
Oh, listen, Harry.

02:22:50.812 --> 02:22:55.317
If that dolt of a cousin of yours,
Dudley, gives you any grief...

02:22:55.567 --> 02:22:58.236
You could always threaten him...

02:22:58.445 --> 02:23:01.323
With a nice pair of ears
to go with his tail.

02:23:01.490 --> 02:23:06.620
But we're not allowed to do magic
away from Hogwarts. You know that.

02:23:07.079 --> 02:23:11.416
I do. But your cousin don't, do he?

02:23:16.922 --> 02:23:20.008
Feels strange to be going home,
doesn't it?

02:23:20.258 --> 02:23:22.344
I'm not going home.

02:23:22.511 --> 02:23:24.471
Not really.